{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:AppendixQvalues.QbetaCkTruncationCanonical","@type":"LeanModule","name":"AppendixQvalues.QbetaCkTruncationCanonical","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_ck_truncation_canonical_conjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_ck_truncation_canonical_conjecture","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L75-L88","doc":"**The conjecture, axiomatised.** There exists a coefficient family `c`\nfor which the canonical-`c_k` class holds — i.e. only `c_2` is proved\nexact, `c_3` is the Hopf near-match, and a canonical anchor-independent\nclosed form for the `c_{k≥3}` exists. The `sorry` IS the conjecture\n(the open Habiro-element identification), per the §3b convention for\nLean formalisation of conjectures. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalExists.exists_c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalExists.exists_c","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The external input: there exists a canonical coefficient family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalExists.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalExists.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalExists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalExists","kind":"class","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L71-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalClass.canonical_ck_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalClass.canonical_ck_exists","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L69-L69","doc":"OPEN conjecture: for `k ≥ 3` the coefficients admit a single\nanchor-independent canonical closed form `f`. This is the conjecture\nproper; an instance's witness for it is conjectural (`sorry`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalClass.c3_near_match_jones_hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalClass.c3_near_match_jones_hopf","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L65-L65","doc":"NEAR-MATCH rung: `c_3` resembles `J_Hopf(q=1) = -2`. Recorded as the\nframework's structural near-match, not a Taylor identity; the actual\nempirical `c_3` is anchor-dependent (3.47% m_p-pin swing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalClass.c2_proved_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalClass.c2_proved_exact","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L61-L61","doc":"PROVED rung: `c_2 = -1` is Taylor-exact (q₀-stable). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QbetaCkTruncationCanonicalClass","kind":"class","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L50-L69","doc":"**Conjecture class for the `Q_β` truncation coefficients** (§3b-cond).\n\nCarries the tiered status of the ladder coefficients `c_k` as class\nfields. The `c_2` and `c_3` fields pin the proved / near-match facts;\nthe `canonical_ck_exists` field is the OPEN conjecture — that for\n`k ≥ 3` there is a single anchor-independent closed form for the `c_k`.\nAny instance discharging `canonical_ck_exists` does so by a `sorry`\nthat IS the conjecture (not a missing proof). No unconditional\ninstance is provided. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical","label":"conj:qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalCkForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalCkForm","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L42-L48","doc":"Predicate naming the property a coefficient family must have to be\n\"canonical\": a single `q₀`-anchor-independent closed form `f : ℕ → ℝ`\n(a constant function of the anchor) realises every `c_k`. We model\nanchor-independence by requiring the realiser to depend only on the\nrung index `k`, not on the substrate parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopfClassicalLimitCk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopfClassicalLimitCk","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/qbeta-ck-truncation-canonical.lean#L38-L40","doc":"Classical-limit Hopf-link Jones value `J_Hopf(q=1) = -2`, the\nnear-match target for `c_3`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}